# T-977: Match on unit constructor using qualified dot-access patterns.
# Color.Green: in match arm position → Pattern::Constructor { tag: "Color.Green", binding: None }.
# Scrutinee Color.Green has Variant tag "Color.Green" — tag equality holds, arm matches.
# After T-1193, constructors are accessed via Color.Red/Color.Green/Color.Blue (qualified form).
#
# Note: no non-exhaustive warning for this case — Color type uses TypeTag patterns (bare uppercase
# like Color.Red:) which the coverage checker doesn't enumerate. B-344 tracks the remaining gap
# where qualified Constructor patterns in nested dicts aren't recognized as covering.
[
  Color: [type Red Green Blue]
  result: [match Color.Green
    Color.Red:   "red"
    Color.Green: "green"
    Color.Blue:  "blue"]
]

=== out
Dict({"Color": Dict({"Red": Variant(Color.Red, Null), "Green": Variant(Color.Green, Null), "Blue": Variant(Color.Blue, Null)}), "result": String("green")})
